### Route & Stop API — manual tests
### VS Code + REST Client extension. Click "Send Request" above any block.
### Test ids match docs/api-test-plan.md.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
# @baseUrl = https://school-bus-route-stop.vercel.app

### Log in through the Schedule & Arrival service first, then paste the
### tokens here. Never commit real tokens.
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN
@parentToken = PASTE_PARENT_TOKEN
@internalKey = PASTE_INTERNAL_API_KEY

### Filled in from the responses as you go.
@routeId = PASTE_ROUTE_ID
@stopId = PASTE_STOP_ID
@busId = PASTE_BUS_ID
@tripId = PASTE_TRIP_ID


### T01 health — no login needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### T02 readiness — proves the database is reachable
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ready

### T03 list routes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T04 ranked search: the exact code comes first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/routes?search=R-01
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T05 create a route
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-route-001

{
  "code": "R-09",
  "name": "Rehab City Line",
  "area": "New Cairo"
}

### T44 same key, same body — replayed, no second route
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-route-001

{
  "code": "R-09",
  "name": "Rehab City Line",
  "area": "New Cairo"
}

### T41 same key, different body — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-route-001

{
  "code": "R-10",
  "name": "Different Line",
  "area": "New Cairo"
}

### T06 add stops (run three times, changing the name)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes/{{routeId}}/stops
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rehab Gate 1",
  "landmark": "Opposite the mosque"
}

### T07 reorder every stop at once
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/routes/{{routeId}}/stops/order
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stop_ids": ["PASTE_ID_3", "PASTE_ID_1", "PASTE_ID_2"]
}

### T07b move a single stop to the front
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/routes/{{routeId}}/stops/order
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "move": { "stop_id": "{{stopId}}", "to_position": 1 }
}

### T21 a partial list is refused — 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/routes/{{routeId}}/stops/order
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stop_ids": ["{{stopId}}"]
}

### T08 delete a stop — the gap closes
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/stops/{{stopId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T23 stop_order cannot be set directly — 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/stops/{{stopId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stop_order": 9
}

### T09 add a bus
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/buses
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "plate_number": "ABC 1234",
  "capacity": 40,
  "route_id": "{{routeId}}"
}

### T10 set the recurring pattern: Sun-Thu mornings
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/routes/{{routeId}}/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "run_type": "morning",
  "days_of_week": [7, 1, 2, 3, 4],
  "bus_id": "{{busId}}",
  "active_from": "2026-03-01"
}

### T26 day 0 does not exist — 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/routes/{{routeId}}/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "run_type": "morning",
  "days_of_week": [0],
  "active_from": "2026-03-01"
}

### T11 preview the generated trips — nothing is written
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from": "2026-03-01",
  "to": "2026-03-14",
  "dry_run": true
}

### T12 commit them
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: generate-march-2026

{
  "from": "2026-03-01",
  "to": "2026-03-14",
  "dry_run": false
}

### T13 search trips by route and day
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/trips?route_id={{routeId}}&date=2026-03-01
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T36 the slot is taken now — 409 ROUTE_SLOT_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "route_id": "{{routeId}}",
  "bus_id": "{{busId}}",
  "service_date": "2026-03-01",
  "run_type": "morning"
}

### T20 a date in the past — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "route_id": "{{routeId}}",
  "service_date": "2020-01-01",
  "run_type": "morning"
}

### T14 who a cancellation would affect
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/{{tripId}}/impact
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T15 cancel the trip — writes the outbox event in the same transaction
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/{{tripId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "cancelled",
  "reason": "Bus 14 is in for repair"
}

### T40 cancelling twice — 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/{{tripId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "cancelled",
  "reason": "Again"
}

### T16 name too short — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "R-11",
  "name": "ab",
  "area": "Maadi"
}

### T17 the client tries to choose the id — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "HACKED-1",
  "code": "R-12",
  "name": "Injected Line",
  "area": "Maadi"
}

### T25 malformed JSON (trailing comma) — 400, server stays up
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "R-13",
  "name": "Broken Line",
  "area": "Maadi",
}

### T42 not JSON — 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: text/plain

code=R-14

### T24 limit above the cap — 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/routes?limit=100000
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T27 no token — 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/routes

### T28 an invented token — 401, same message as T27
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer this-token-was-never-issued-aaaaaaaa

### T29 a parent trying to create a route — 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{parentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "R-15",
  "name": "Parent Should Not Create This",
  "area": "Maadi"
}

### T30 a parent trying to delete — 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/routes/{{routeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{parentToken}}

### T33 an id that does not exist — 404 RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "cancelled",
  "reason": "No such trip"
}

### T34 a path that does not exist — 404 ROUTE_NOT_FOUND (different code)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/nonsense
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T31 internal endpoint with no key — 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/internal/events

### T50 the outbox, with the service key
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/internal/events
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### T51 acknowledge an event (what the forwarder does)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/internal/events/ack
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_ids": ["PASTE_EVENT_ID"]
}

### T49 the scheduled run, as Vercel Cron calls it
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/internal/cron/generate?days=21
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### T48 a preflight from a hostile origin — no allow header comes back
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Origin: https://evil.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST

### T47 a preflight from the real frontend — allowed
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/api/routes
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
